WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.523
Government Office.

2
00:00:01.803 --> 00:00:06.155
Day 53 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:07.905 --> 00:00:08.929
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:20.345
Today's goal: handle passport, ID card, driving licence and other government work: asking which documents you need, which counter to go to, and following up on applications.

5
00:00:21.695 --> 00:00:22.549
Part 1.

6
00:00:22.829 --> 00:00:23.789
Key words.

7
00:00:25.039 --> 00:00:26.404
Here is a quick table:

8
00:00:26.684 --> 00:00:46.908
Word or phrase, and Meaning. application or form or appointment slot: what you submit or book. documents or proof of address or ID proof: papers you need. original or photocopy or self-attested: the real one or copy or copy signed by you. token number or counter or window: queue system.

9
00:00:47.188 --> 00:00:59.177
verification or police verification: checking your details. status or acknowledgement or receipt number: where your application is or proof you applied. fee or challan: payment.

10
00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:01.402
Part 2.

11
00:01:01.682 --> 00:01:02.898
Questions you'll ask.

12
00:01:04.148 --> 00:01:06.815
Which documents do I need for a passport renewal?

13
00:01:07.095 --> 00:01:09.804
Do I need originals, or are photocopies enough?

14
00:01:10.084 --> 00:01:11.684
Which counter should I go to?

15
00:01:11.964 --> 00:01:13.841
How long does it take to process?

16
00:01:14.121 --> 00:01:16.489
How can I check the status of my application?

17
00:01:16.769 --> 00:01:17.815
Is there a fee?

18
00:01:18.095 --> 00:01:19.225
How do I pay it?

19
00:01:19.505 --> 00:01:21.575
Can someone else submit it on my behalf?

20
00:01:22.925 --> 00:01:25.101
What should I do if a document is missing?

21
00:01:26.451 --> 00:01:27.347
Part 3.

22
00:01:27.627 --> 00:01:28.992
Questions you'll be asked.

23
00:01:30.242 --> 00:01:31.607
Here is a quick table:

24
00:01:31.887 --> 00:01:33.423
They ask, and You answer.

25
00:01:33.703 --> 00:01:35.239
What's your application number?:

26
00:01:35.519 --> 00:01:40.255
It's PSK-2026 to 11823.

27
00:01:40.535 --> 00:01:41.751
Here's the printout.

28
00:01:42.031 --> 00:01:43.397
Do you have the originals?:

29
00:01:43.677 --> 00:01:44.829
Yes, here they are.

30
00:01:45.109 --> 00:01:46.495
Has your address changed?:

31
00:01:46.775 --> 00:01:48.397
Yes, I moved last year.

32
00:01:48.677 --> 00:01:50.277
Here's my rental agreement.

33
00:01:50.557 --> 00:01:51.773
Sign here, please.:

34
00:01:52.053 --> 00:01:53.525
(Sign.) Is that all?

35
00:01:54.875 --> 00:01:55.792
Part 4.

36
00:01:56.072 --> 00:01:58.568
Conversation 1: at the passport office.

37
00:01:59.818 --> 00:02:01.845
Here is how the conversation goes.

38
00:02:02.125 --> 00:02:03.255
Token number?

39
00:02:03.535 --> 00:02:05.349
A-142.

40
00:02:05.629 --> 00:02:07.741
I'm here for a passport renewal.

41
00:02:08.021 --> 00:02:09.813
Here's my appointment letter.

42
00:02:10.093 --> 00:02:12.354
Old passport and documents, please.

43
00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:16.687
Here's the old passport, my Aadhaar card, and the address proof.

44
00:02:16.967 --> 00:02:19.442
Your address is different from the old passport.

45
00:02:20.792 --> 00:02:22.392
The conversation continues.

46
00:02:22.672 --> 00:02:24.592
Yes, I've moved to Bengaluru.

47
00:02:24.872 --> 00:02:28.243
Here's the rental agreement and an electricity bill.

48
00:02:28.523 --> 00:02:30.955
The electricity bill is in the owner's name.

49
00:02:31.235 --> 00:02:32.941
Do you have anything in your name?

50
00:02:33.221 --> 00:02:35.739
I have my bank statement with this address.

51
00:02:36.019 --> 00:02:37.213
Will that work?

52
00:02:37.493 --> 00:02:38.773
Yes, that's fine.

53
00:02:39.053 --> 00:02:41.848
Please go to counter B for photos and fingerprints.

54
00:02:43.198 --> 00:02:44.798
The conversation continues.

55
00:02:45.078 --> 00:02:46.017
Thank you.

56
00:02:46.297 --> 00:02:48.601
How long will it take to get the passport?

57
00:02:48.881 --> 00:02:51.889
After police verification, about two to three weeks.

58
00:02:52.169 --> 00:02:53.961
How can I check the status?

59
00:02:54.241 --> 00:02:55.969
Online, with your file number.

60
00:02:56.249 --> 00:02:57.699
It's on this receipt.

61
00:02:59.049 --> 00:03:00.009
Part 5.

62
00:03:00.289 --> 00:03:02.807
Conversation 2: following up by phone.

63
00:03:04.057 --> 00:03:06.083
Here is how the conversation goes.

64
00:03:06.363 --> 00:03:07.451
Good morning.

65
00:03:07.731 --> 00:03:13.875
I applied for a driving licence renewal a month ago, but the status still says under process.

66
00:03:14.155 --> 00:03:15.798
What's your application number?

67
00:03:16.078 --> 00:03:20.238
DL-RN-554210.

68
00:03:20.518 --> 00:03:21.627
Let me check...

69
00:03:21.907 --> 00:03:23.955
It's waiting for the officer's approval.

70
00:03:24.235 --> 00:03:26.795
Is there anything missing from my side?

71
00:03:28.145 --> 00:03:29.745
The conversation continues.

72
00:03:30.025 --> 00:03:31.924
No, the documents are complete.

73
00:03:32.204 --> 00:03:34.871
Could you tell me roughly when it will be approved?

74
00:03:35.151 --> 00:03:36.793
Within ten working days.

75
00:03:37.073 --> 00:03:38.012
Thank you.

76
00:03:38.292 --> 00:03:41.513
If there's no update by then, who should I contact?

77
00:03:41.793 --> 00:03:45.313
You can email the RTO helpdesk with your application number.

78
00:03:46.663 --> 00:03:47.602
Part 6.

79
00:03:47.882 --> 00:03:48.586
Tips.

80
00:03:49.836 --> 00:03:54.359
Carry originals + two photocopies of everything, and passport-size photos.

81
00:03:54.639 --> 00:03:57.668
Write down token, file and application numbers.

82
00:03:57.948 --> 00:03:59.505
Stay polite and patient.

83
00:03:59.785 --> 00:04:03.732
Could you please help me understand what's missing? works better than arguing.

84
00:04:05.082 --> 00:04:06.021
Part 7.

85
00:04:06.301 --> 00:04:07.346
Speak today.

86
00:04:08.596 --> 00:04:13.737
Make a list in English of your important documents (ID, address proof, certificates).

87
00:04:14.017 --> 00:04:14.935
Practise:

88
00:04:15.215 --> 00:04:18.564
Which documents do I need? and How can I check the status?

89
00:04:19.914 --> 00:04:21.450
That's the end of this lesson.

90
00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:26.402
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

91
00:04:26.682 --> 00:04:32.783
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

